/*
  Currency.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0083 · Currency (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. The web source
  (components/data-display/format/Currency.tsx) renders NO translatable copy: it
  makes no `t()` call. It displays only a monetary figure — the user's preferred
  currency symbol (itself a setting, not this component's copy) prefixed onto a
  locale-formatted number — or, for a null / non-finite value, the caller-supplied
  `fallback` (a locale-neutral em dash by default, exactly as the web prop default
  is). There are therefore no message keys to mirror, and the Swift sources hold no
  English literals.

  The surface's only locale-sensitive output is the number itself: grouping
  separators and the decimal mark. That localization is bound through the injected
  `Locale` (CurrencyInput.locale → CurrencyFormatting.number), the native parity of
  the web `fmtNumber` global-locale read, rather than through a string table. The
  per-surface table name ("Currency") is reserved here so the file-set stays
  consistent with its sibling surfaces and folds into the app `Localizable.xcstrings`
  master catalog at integration time should localizable chrome ever be added.
*/
